Are you strong in planning, organizing, and maintaining oversight in a dynamic logistics environment? Do you enjoy improving processes while supporting a fast-growing operation? Then the role of Operations Planner in Moerdijk could be your next career move. Working in one of the largest and most modern warehouses in the Benelux, you will play a crucial role in ensuring the smooth flow of daily order operations. You will make sure everything behind the scenes is perfectly coordinated, allowing the operation to perform at its best.

As an Operations Planner, you will be responsible for the warehouse's outbound planning activities. You will ensure that customer orders are properly prepared, scheduled, and processed within the operation. Working closely with the operational teams, you will act as a key link between systems, planning, and execution.

Your responsibilities include:

- Processing daily customer requests and forecasts;
- Planning and prioritizing outbound orders within the system;
- Aligning capacity and operational activities with the warehouse floor;
- Coordinating pick-and-pack processes to ensure orders are processed efficiently;
- Acting as the first point of contact for operational planning-related questions;
- Monitoring the progress, timing, and accuracy of order flows;
- Ensuring that all process steps are followed strictly from start to finish;
- Supporting the optimization of planning and logistics processes.

For this position, we are looking for someone who excels at planning and can maintain a clear overview in a complex logistics environment.

- Relevant experience within logistics (planning and/or warehouse operations);
- Strong organizational and administrative skills;
- Ability to work under pressure and effectively prioritize tasks;
- Good command of the English language (required);
- Comfortable working with computers and digital systems;
- Available to work full-time in a two-shift schedule.

Are you experienced in a warehouse and ready to take the next step into a leadership role? Or do you already have some experience in supervising colleagues and want to further develop yourself as a team leader? Then this is your opportunity! Within a fast-growing and international logistics environment, you will have the opportunity to further develop your leadership skills and  take on more responsibility step by step.

As a (junior) Warehouse Team Leader, you will work alongside an experienced team and supervise a group of 10 to 12 employees. You will be visibly present on the work floor, supporting the daily coordination of operations. You work closely with the Supervisor and be given the space to grow in your role.

Your responsibilities include:

- Supporting the supervision and guidance of warehouse employees;
- Working on the floor to ensure smooth daily operations;
- Identifying operational bottlenecks and discussing them with your manager;
- Contributing to the improvement of work processes;
- Monitoring basic safety and quality regulations;
- Working with simple reports and developing basic Excel skills.

We are primarily looking for someone with the right motivation and ambition to grow into a leadership role within logistics. In addition, you have:

- Experience in a warehouse or logistics environment;
- Interest in supervising or guiding colleagues;
- Good command of the English language (required);
- Basic knowledge of Excel or willingness to learn;
- A proactive and eager-to-learn attitude;
- Availability to work full-time in a two-shift system.

Have you not yet held a full team leader position, but do you have ambition and some initial experience in leading others? We strongly encourage you to apply.
